From: Caboose <caboose@local>
Subject: [PATCH 77/77] Give every dispatchable object its executor generation

A process outlives its executor: the phone leaves and returns, and the process connects to
the new executor with its next instance. Its old objects did not go with the old executor:
once another thread had reconnected, a call on a pre-loss device, queue, command buffer or
physical device was encoded to the new executor, which does not know its handles (an
unboxing failure ends the executor) or knows them as other objects. Each dispatchable object
now records the executor generation it was made under (caboose::completion::
connectionGeneration, one more for each executor after a loss), and every encoder entry
reports VK_ERROR_DEVICE_LOST for an object of an earlier generation without touching the
stream; the application rebuilds on the new executor.

Answers and tables of the previous executor that were kept for the process are forgotten on
the new generation through one reset hook (caboose::completion::onNewGeneration): the cached
memory types, heaps and budget, the instance extension table, the device features the driver
emulates around, the devices' presentation queues, completion watches owed to old queues
and host allocations shared through dma-bufs. A device's presentation queue is forgotten
with the device.
---
